@startuml 10-exceptions
!include _style.iuml
title Exception hierarchy and HTTP mapping
left to right direction

class RuntimeException
abstract class IitsmException {
  - status : HttpStatus
  + getStatus() : HttpStatus
}
class GlobalExceptionHandler <<@RestControllerAdvice>> {
  turns any exception into ApiError JSON
}
class ApiError <<record>> {
  timestamp, status, error,
  message, path, fieldErrors
}

RuntimeException <|-- IitsmException
IitsmException <|-- InvalidInputException : 400
IitsmException <|-- InvalidCredentialsException : 401
IitsmException <|-- UnauthorizedOperationException : 403
IitsmException <|-- ResourceNotFoundException : 404
IitsmException <|-- IncidentNotFoundException : 404
IitsmException <|-- ServiceNotFoundException : 404
IitsmException <|-- InvalidStateTransitionException : 409
IitsmException <|-- DuplicateResourceException : 409
IitsmException <|-- DuplicateIncidentException : 409
IitsmException <|-- TechnicianUnavailableException : 422
IitsmException <|-- WorkloadExceededException : 422
IitsmException <|-- MissingSlaConfigurationException : 500
GlobalExceptionHandler ..> IitsmException : handles
GlobalExceptionHandler ..> ApiError : returns
@enduml
